From 575eea7208b4cf10228121222e02dc7163b0d5a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seris <zihlingchen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:20:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Convert to a plain Vite + React SPA for static hosting on
 Vercel

Replaces the TanStack Start / SSR setup with a standard Vite single-page
app. `vite build` now emits a fully static bundle to dist/ with no server
entry and no platform adapter.

Removed:
- TanStack Start, TanStack Router and the generated route tree
- src/server.ts and src/start.ts (SSR entry, request/function middleware)
- the nitro build target and @lovable.dev/vite-tanstack-config, which
  defaulted to Cloudflare, plus the wrangler/Cloudflare ignore rules
- server-only Supabase modules that can no longer run anywhere: the
  service-role client, the auth middleware, the serverFn auth attacher
  and the cron authenticator
- the SSR error-capture/error-page pair

Added:
- index.html + src/main.tsx as the SPA entry, with the site-wide document
  head that the root route's head() used to render
- React Router v7 (createBrowserRouter) in src/App.tsx
- ProtectedRoute, the client-side equivalent of the _authenticated route's
  beforeLoad guard
- usePageMeta, the client-side stand-in for per-route head()
- vercel.json with a rewrite to /index.html so deep links resolve
  client-side

Routes: / (landing), /sign-in and /sign-up (the combined auth page, path
picks the tab), /login redirecting to /sign-in, /app (auth-gated, was
/barbers), and a catch-all 404.

UI, styling and the Supabase auth flow are unchanged. The Supabase client
drops its process.env fallback and reads only the VITE_ variables, which
Vite inlines at build time.

The bun lockfile was regenerated against registry.npmjs.org; it previously
pinned tarballs to a Lovable-internal npm cache that a Vercel build cannot
reach.

